# Pal runners and DI ports

## Runner structs implement pal.Runner

A struct named `Runner` or `runner` MUST implement `pal.Runner` (`Run(ctx context.Context) error`).

Do not name library/orchestrator types `Runner` / `runner` unless they are the pal lifecycle entrypoint. Prefer role names (`CodeGenerator`, `GoModWrapper`, …).

Unexported `runner` for a subcommand entrypoint is fine when it implements `Run`.

## No proxy runners

Do not introduce a pal runner whose `Run` only forwards to another component.

Put CLI-bound fields on the component that does the work and make **that** type the runner. Dual entry on the same type is OK (e.g. `Run` for CLI + `Sync(ctx, req)` for programmatic callers).

```go
// BAD — thin proxy
func (r *runner) Run(ctx context.Context) error {
	return r.ProjectSyncer.Sync(ctx, core.SyncRequest{Dir: r.Dir})
}

// GOOD — component is the runner
func (s *ProjectSyncer) Run(ctx context.Context) error {
	return s.Sync(ctx, core.SyncRequest{Dir: s.Dir, FormaReplace: s.FormaReplace, AddComponents: s.AddComponents})
}
```

## Ports and main implementations share the role name

Cross-package DI ports live in `internal/core`. The main concrete type in the implementing package uses the **same** name as the port (not `Service`, `Tool`, or `adapter`).

| Port | Package type | Main method(s) |
|------|--------------|----------------|
| `GoModWrapper` | `gotool.GoModWrapper` | `InitModule`, `Require`, `Replace`, `Tidy` |
| `NpmWrapper` | `webtool.NpmWrapper` | `Install` |
| `ShadcnWrapper` | `webtool.ShadcnWrapper` | `Add` |
| `CodeGenerator` | `codegen.CodeGenerator` | `Generate` |
| `ProjectSyncer` | `synccmd.ProjectSyncer` | `Sync` (+ `Run` when it is the sync CLI entry) |

Multi-method ports are fine when they wrap one toolchain (`GoModWrapper`). Split when tools are independent (npm vs shadcn).

## Method verbs vs pal lifecycle

Prefer short verb method names on ports. Do **not** use pal lifecycle names on non-runner collaborators: `Init`, `Run`, `Shutdown`, `HealthCheck` (or `Pal*` twins).

`go mod init` → `InitModule` (not `Init`). `Run` belongs only on intentional `pal.Runner` types.

